id: pm-wmf72c
title: "Evolution is unrecorded: one supersedes edge exists across 1799 closed items and 14 releases, so nothing in the graph says which work replaced which"
description: "Measured 2026-07-27 from pm graph audit profile.edges_by_kind. The corpus holds 9262 edges. Exactly one of them is supersedes. Two are incident_from. 161 are discovered_from. Against 1799 closed items spanning 14 released versions and roughly two months of dense daily work, that distribution says the tracker has recorded almost no evolution at all. The kinds that exist to express replacement, derivation and causation are the kinds that carry a project through time, and they are the three rarest in the graph while related, a kind with no direction and no semantics, accounts for 4437 edges or 48 percent. The effect is concrete and checkable. This project has repeatedly superseded its own decisions: an ADR is accepted and a later one revises it, a command spelling is consolidated into a noun and the old spelling survives as an alias, an audit surface is extracted into a package and the in-core version is removed, a measurement script is replaced by a canonical one. Every one of those transitions is described in prose inside a resolution or a close reason, and none of them is an edge. A reader can find them only by reading text, which is exactly the cost the graph exists to remove. The same is true of derivation: work discovered while doing other work is the dominant way items are born here, and 161 discovered_from edges cannot account for 2118 items. Retyping is not the whole answer and should not be forced, because a related edge between two items that merely mention each other is honest. The gap is that no evidence pipeline exists to promote the cases where the relationship is stated in durable text into the kind that states it structurally."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags[7]: "area:graph","area:sdk",context-management,governance,history,relationships,traceability
created_at: "2026-07-27T04:08:01.532Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-27T04:21:39.253Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 420
acceptance_criteria: "Replacement, derivation and causation relationships stated in durable text such as resolutions, close reasons, duplicate closures and history messages are promotable to typed edges by an evidence rule, not by judgement per item; Promotion is auditable: every typed edge created this way records the evidence class that produced it and remains reversible without losing the prior version; A related edge that genuinely carries no direction stays related; the pass never retypes for the sake of the distribution; The typed-kind distribution is a reported governance metric, so a corpus where supersedes is vanishingly rare is a visible condition rather than an unexamined default; Traversal over the promoted kinds answers the question of what replaced what across releases without reading item prose"
goal: project management = context management
objective: Recover the projects evolution as typed structure so graph algorithms can trace replacement and derivation lineages across the full history
value: Superseded work is the largest silent category in a mature tracker; without lineage edges an agent rereads obsolete decisions and cannot tell that a newer one governs
impact: "Directly serves the deep-linking requirement: lineage edges are what create long typed chains through terminal history rather than a wide flat rim of associations"
why_now: "The terminal backfill connected the corpus and left related at 48 percent of all edges, which the backfill evidence itself flagged as the bucket to refine rather than a settled default"
parent: pm-96h7
risk: medium
confidence: high
severity: medium
environment: "pm 2026.7.27, this workspace at 2118 items, measured via pm graph audit --summary profile.edges_by_kind"
repro_steps: "Run pm graph audit --json and read profile.edges_by_kind; compare the supersedes, incident_from and discovered_from counts against by_status.closed from pm stats"
expected_result: A tracker with 1799 closed items over 14 releases records many replacement and derivation relationships as typed edges
actual_result: "supersedes 1, incident_from 2, discovered_from 161, against related 4437"
