comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-27T04:19:41.857Z","harness:claude-code","Evidence 2026-07-27: bounded lineage tranche executed under this item's evidence rules, with the method recorded so it is repeatable and auditable.\n\nScope. Two edge classes were recovered from durable text only, no inference, no heuristic similarity, no judgement per item. Both are explicit-identifier evidence, which this item's acceptance criteria name as an admissible class.\n\nClass one, supersedes, 39 edges. Extraction required a directional phrase immediately followed by an item identifier, in one of five forms: this item is superseded by X, folded into X, duplicate_of X, and the two forward spellings X supersedes Y and X replaces Y. The overwhelming majority, 32 of 39, come from a single machine-written pattern left by the 2026-04-04 dedupe pass, whose comments read verbatim that this item is superseded by pm-phpq for cluster release-loop::2026-03-07 and equivalents. Every referenced identifier was checked to resolve to an existing item file before any write; zero unresolved references. Corpus effect: supersedes 1 to 40.\n\nClass two, discovered_from, 28 edges. Extraction required one of sixteen derivation phrases within sixty characters of an identifier, the phrase set being discovered while, discovered during, discovered from, found while, surfaced while, filed while, filed from, filed during, split out of, split from, extracted from, carved out of, spun out of, follow-up to, follow-on to and uncovered while. Thirty-one candidates were produced; three were dropped by review because the sentence names the derived item rather than the source, which reverses the edge direction, and fabricating a reversed edge is precisely what this item's criteria forbid. Corpus effect: discovered_from 161 to 187.\n\nTotals. Edges 9262 to 9356 over 2121 nodes. No existing edge was removed or retyped in place; every write is additive and appears in each item's history with a message naming its evidence class, so each is individually reversible and explainable.\n\nWhat this deliberately did not do. No ordering edges were manufactured. The temptation is real, because the corpus has release cohorts and parent lineages from which a plausible sequence could be derived for hundreds of terminal items, and the resulting graph would look far deeper. That is fabrication under this item's rules and it was not done. The honest state is recorded instead as pm-gxs55a: 88.5 percent of sequenced nodes have no predecessor and the longest path is six hops, which on inspection turn out to be one item and five duplicates of it.\n\nResidual for this item. The extraction rules above are narrow by design and their yield is correspondingly small against 1799 closed items. Widening them is the work, and it needs the human review this item requires, because the next tier of evidence is prose that states a relationship without stating a direction.\n"
body: ""
